      {
        "entry_id": "sqli-error-message",
        "technique": "error-based",
        "text": "{\"detection_method\": \"Inspect the candidate response for a SQL syntax diagnostic and distinguish it from a generic application error or an error already present in the normal response.\", \"functional_semantics\": \"A malformed SQL literal can expose a database-specific parser message. Such a message helps infer SQL context without reading application source.\", \"limitations\": \"Error wording depends on engine, version and application error handling. Fingerprinting alone does not establish successful exploitation or a target vulnerability label.\", \"title\": \"Interpret database-specific returned errors\", \"vulnerability_type\": \"error-based\"}",
        "text_sha256": "25d35835a70015d667db7e30f92cde99525e713ff6c6e86b0e48279a2e0c1c0c",
