      {
        "entry_id": "sqli-time-repeated",
        "technique": "time-based blind",
        "text": "{\"detection_method\": \"Use repeated candidate and no-delay control measurements at the same input. Compare their timing separation rather than treating a single slow response as proof. This repeated-control procedure is an editorial adaptation.\", \"functional_semantics\": \"A controlled conditional database delay should track predicate evaluation; unrelated network or server delay can produce slow HTTP responses without SQL injection.\", \"limitations\": \"Timing variance and timeouts can mask the difference. The source examples do not prescribe this project's decision threshold, repetitions, or ground-truth labels.\", \"title\": \"Repeated timing comparison with a no-delay control\", \"vulnerability_type\": \"time-based blind\"}",
